# November 18, 2026: Fulton County, New York, first close pass (region mohawk, drawn at random by
# tools/choose.py --state ny, which offered Broadalbin). The Atlas had nothing in Johnstown, Gloversville, Mayfield or
# Broadalbin. Johnstown: Johnson Hall, the 1772 courthouse and jail, St. John's church and Sir William Johnson's grave,
# the Colonial Cemetery with the Drumm House, the 1781 battlefield markers, the Knox Mansion. Gloversville: the Glove
# Theatre, the Carnegie library, the armory, the downtown district and the county museum in the Kingsboro school.
# Mayfield: the Rice Homestead and the Log Cabin Church. Broadalbin: the Hotel Broadalbin. On the Sacandaga (region adk,
# like the other Sacandaga places): drowned Fish House and the Shew house, the Caroga museum, Northville's district.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py); parks.ny.gov, HMdb marker pages, 44lakes.com
# (Fulton County tourism), visitsacandaga.com, mohawkvalleymuseums.us, theglovetheatre.com, the Haunted History Trail
# page and carogalake.com through tools/page.py. National Register forms for this county on NPGallery are one-page
# scans with no text and were not read.
